<Base title="About — Transit411">
  <div class="page">
    <h1 class="disp">About Transit411</h1>
    <p class="lede">Transit411 is built by transit professionals, for transit professionals.</p>
    <p>It exists to answer the everyday questions that come up across transit funding, procurement, and program delivery — the kind that usually mean digging through PDFs, agency websites, and databases — and to put the power of AI to work gathering and analyzing that information.</p>

    <h2 class="disp">Why we built it</h2>
    <p>People who work in and around public transit spend an enormous amount of time chasing down the same facts: who's in the FTA funding pipeline, what an agency spends per rider, which procurements are open, who just moved into a new role. The information is public, but it's scattered and slow to assemble. Transit411 pulls it together and makes it answerable in plain English.</p>

    <h2 class="disp">What we do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>The wire</strong> — independent coverage of transit funding, procurement, people, and policy, gathered continuously and curated for the people who need to act on it.</li>
      <li><strong>Ask NTD</strong> — ask the National Transit Database in plain English and get a sourced answer, with the query shown so you can trust it.</li>
      <li><strong>CIG Pipeline &amp; Ask CIG</strong> — the FTA Capital Investment Grants pipeline, tracked month over month, searchable in plain English.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We built the platform to harness AI for the parts machines do well — collecting, structuring, and querying large amounts of public data — while keeping human judgment on what actually matters.</p>

    <h2 class="disp">Who's behind it</h2>
    <p>Transit411 is a product of <strong>Shepherd Labs</strong>, a small team applying modern data and AI tools to the transit industry. Questions, ideas, or corrections are always welcome — <a href="/contact">get in touch</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
